# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITAL Landing — public client environment
#
# This is a Vite app, so ONLY variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the
# browser. (A NEXT_PUBLIC_* name would simply be ignored here — that prefix is
# Next.js-specific, and the landing page is TanStack Start on Vite.)
#
# Everything in this file ships in the client bundle. Never put secrets here:
# no SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, no DATABASE_URL, no Paymob or Anthropic keys. The
# landing page is purely public marketing and talks to no backend at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Origin of the authenticated VITAL web app. Used only to build the
# "Sign In" -> ${VITE_APP_URL}/login and "Get Started" -> ${VITE_APP_URL}/signup
# links. No trailing slash.
#
# Local development (apps/web runs on 3003):
VITE_APP_URL=http://localhost:3003

# Production: set this in the Vercel project settings to your real app origin,
# e.g. VITE_APP_URL=https://app.your-domain.com
